<figure class="r55-work" aria-labelledby="r55-work-title">
 <figcaption id="r55-work-title"><span>Figure 2</span> LIMIT 5 follows work over many more rows</figcaption>
 <p>Observed PostgreSQL 18.6 plan · separate anonymous 20,000-row fixture · no forced index setting</p>
 <ol><li><strong>GIN finds 200 lexical matches.</strong><span>Bitmap Index Scan on the document index.</span></li><li><strong>The heap scan keeps 100 eligible rows.</strong><span>Stock/shop filtering removes 100; the bitmap contains no lossy heap blocks in this run.</span></li><li><strong>Ranking supplies a sort key for those 100 rows.</strong><span>A top-N heapsort keeps the best 5 by rank descending, then identifier.</span></li><li><strong>The limit returns 5 rows.</strong><span>The index did not return an already ranked top 5.</span></li></ol>
</figure>
